## RaceGOW5 Track 1

    Series      RaceGOW, an at home whoop time trial series
    Track       RaceGOW5 Track 1, designed by Skittles
    Source      racegow.com/tracks, the official Track 1 animation
    Held at     src/room-data.js, generated by scripts/bake-room.js

The fifth act flies a real published track rather than an invented one. What
is reproduced is a set of DIMENSIONS: where a gate stands, how high its sill
is, and which side of a pole the line goes. RaceGOW publishes its tracks
precisely so that everybody can build them, which is the whole premise of the
series, and the credit here is the one the series itself gives: the designer
by name, and the organiser's own figures for the pipe and the opening.

The numbers are not read from RaceGOW directly. They come from
`Mathew-Harvey/WebFPVSimulator`, which is the copy of record for this project
and carries its own citations in `src/trackbuilder/racegow.js` and
`src/trackbuilder/presets.js`, and the simulator credits andAgainFPV for
bringing the track over. Regenerate rather than edit, so the front door and
the simulator cannot come to disagree about where a gate is.

## Zen Kaku Gothic New, Caveat Brush and M PLUS Rounded 1c

    Zen Kaku Gothic New   The Zen Kaku Gothic Project Authors
                          https://github.com/googlefonts/zen-kakugothic
    Caveat Brush          Impallari Type
                          https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Caveat+Brush
    M PLUS Rounded 1c     The M+ Fonts Project, Coji Morishita
                          https://fonts.google.com/specimen/M+PLUS+Rounded+1c
    Licence               SIL Open Font License 1.1, all three
    Held at               stickers/index.html, base64 in its #fontcss block,
                          and src/stickers-data.js, generated from it

These are the three faces the sticker pack sets its type in, subsetted and
embedded so that the pack is one file that prints from a desk and so that
the stickers the film wears at / are set from the same bytes a printer gets.
The pack carries M PLUS Rounded 1c under its earlier name, Rounded Mplus 1c,
as well: same bytes, two names, so a sticker set in either resolves.

The OFL is not the GPL and does not need to be: it permits embedding a font
in a document and redistributing the document, which is all that is done
here, and the fonts are not sold on their own. The subsets travel under
their own names because they are used only as embedded web fonts, which is
the use the OFL's naming clause and the Google Fonts distribution of these
faces both contemplate. Nothing here is relicensed.

